From 6761845ff5228d617bfb3190b269ce537a1f9838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:49:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(carry): fixtures read the carried stock; lathe carry
 refused by name; carried body cached

- A carried setup's tagged fixtures are read against the body it is
  entered with: a fixture standing inside material the earlier setups
  left refuses the post by name (fixture_carried::FIXTURE_IN_CARRIED);
  one seated on a face they machined is clear even where the declared
  block still reaches through it. Live at the post gate.
- The lathe / mill-turn part flip stays refused, now one named constant
  (stock_sim::CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL), pinned on generation, the rest
  chain, the sim and the post.
- The carried body is memoized by content (origin stock, lattice, turns,
  every cutting atom's exact moves), bounded, cleared with the document;
  rest::carried_body_computes pins that an unrelated edit is a hit and an
  upstream one recomputes.

Fixes #321

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
